    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    M = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    # Store all edges as (cost, u, v)\n    edges = []\n    # We'll also keep track of the operations to build the graph\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n        C = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n        A = []\n        for _ in range(K):\n            A.append(int(data[idx])); idx += 1\n        \n        # For each pair in A, add an edge with weight C\n        # But directly adding all pairs would be too slow (K can be up to N, total K sum <= 4e5)\n        # Instead, we can treat each operation as: all vertices in A are connected to each other with weight C\n        # This is equivalent to a \"virtual node\" connecting all of them with cost C\n        # But since we need MST, we can use Kruskal's algorithm with a trick:\n        # For each operation, connect all vertices in A to the first vertex in A with cost C\n        # Then the MST will naturally include the necessary edges.\n        # This is a standard technique to handle \"clique\" additions without enumerating all pairs.\n        \n        # However, we must be careful: if we connect each vertex to the first,\n        # we might create cycles within the operation, but Kruskal's algorithm will ignore them\n        # because we sort edges by cost and use union-find.\n        # So we can add edges: (C, A[0], A[i]) for i from 1 to K-1\n        \n        if K >= 2:\n            # Add edges from first vertex to each other vertex\n            for i in range(1, K):\n                edges.append((C, A[0]-1, A[i]-1))  # convert to 0-indexed\n    \n    # Now run Kruskal's algorithm\n    parent = list(range(N))\n    rank = [0] * N\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        xroot = find(x)\n        yroot = find(y)\n        if xroot == yroot:\n            return False\n        if rank[xroot] < rank[yroot]:\n            parent[xroot] = yroot\n        elif rank[xroot] > rank[yroot]:\n            parent[yroot] = xroot\n        else:\n            parent[yroot] = xroot\n            rank[xroot] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    # Sort edges by cost\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    total_cost = 0\n    edges_used = 0\n    \n    for cost, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            total_cost += cost\n            edges_used += 1\n            if edges_used == N - 1:\n                break\n    \n    # Check if graph is connected\n    if edges_used != N - 1:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(total_cost)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
