    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef mod_inverse(a, mod):\n    return pow(a, mod - 2, mod)\n\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import deque\n\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W = map(int, data[0].split())\n    grid = [list(line.strip()) for line in data[1:1+H]]\n\n    # Count red cells and find green connected components\n    red_count = 0\n    green_cells = []\n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    components = 0\n\n    # Directions for adjacent cells\n    dirs = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\n\n    # Find all green connected components\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                green_cells.append((i, j))\n                if not visited[i][j]:\n                    components += 1\n                    queue = deque([(i, j)])\n                    visited[i][j] = True\n                    while queue:\n                        x, y = queue.popleft()\n                        for dx, dy in dirs:\n                            nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n                            if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and grid[nx][ny] == '#' and not visited[nx][ny]:\n                                visited[nx][ny] = True\n                                queue.append((nx, ny))\n            else:\n                red_count += 1\n\n    if red_count == 0:\n        print(components)\n        return\n\n    # For each red cell, simulate turning it green and compute change in components\n    total_expected = 0\n\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                # Count how many green neighbors this red cell has\n                neighbors = []\n                for dx, dy in dirs:\n                    ni, nj = i + dx, j + dy\n                    if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W and grid[ni][nj] == '#':\n                        neighbors.append((ni, nj))\n\n                # If no green neighbors, adding this cell creates 1 new component\n                if len(neighbors) == 0:\n                    new_components = components + 1\n                else:\n                    # Find how many distinct green components these neighbors belong to\n                    comp_set = set()\n                    # We need to know which component each neighbor belongs to\n                    # We'll recompute component id for green cells (since we didn't store it before)\n                    comp_id = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]\n                    comp_counter = 0\n                    vis = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n                    for x in range(H):\n                        for y in range(W):\n                            if grid[x][y] == '#' and not vis[x][y]:\n                                queue = deque([(x, y)])\n                                vis[x][y] = True\n                                while queue:\n                                    cx, cy = queue.popleft()\n                                    comp_id[cx][cy] = comp_counter\n                                    for dx2, dy2 in dirs:\n                                        nx, ny = cx + dx2, cy + dy2\n                                        if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and grid[nx][ny] == '#' and not vis[nx][ny]:\n                                            vis[nx][ny] = True\n                                            queue.append((nx, ny))\n                                comp_counter += 1\n\n                    for nx, ny in neighbors:\n                        comp_set.add(comp_id[nx][ny])\n                    # Adding this red cell connects these components\n                    # So we lose (len(neighbors_components) - 1) components\n                    new_components = components - len(comp_set) + 1\n\n                total_expected += new_components\n\n    # Expected value = total_expected / red_count\n    numerator = total_expected % MOD\n    denominator = red_count % MOD\n    result = (numerator * mod_inverse(denominator, MOD)) % MOD\n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
