      "generated_answer": "**Python function**\n\n```python\ndef sum_of_power(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the sum of power of all non‑empty subsets of `nums`,\n    where power of a subset = (max value)^2 * (min value),\n    modulo 10**9+7.\n    \"\"\"\n    MOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\n\n    # ----- 1. frequency of each distinct value -----\n    from collections import Counter\n    cnt = Counter(nums)                 # value -> frequency\n    vals = sorted(cnt)                  # distinct values in increasing order\n    m = len(vals)\n    freqs = [cnt[v] for v in vals]\n\n    # ----- 2. pre‑computations -----\n    # 2^c   and   (2^c - 1) for each distinct value\n    pow2 = [pow(2, c, MOD) for c in freqs]\n    nonempty = [(p - 1) % MOD for p in pow2]          # 2^c - 1  (choose at least one)\n\n    # prefix product of 2^c   (Π_{k=0..i} 2^{c_k})\n    prefix = [0] * m\n    cur = 1\n    for i in range(m):\n        cur = (cur * pow2[i]) % MOD\n        prefix[i] = cur\n\n    # modular inverses of the prefix products\n    inv_prefix = [pow(prefix[i], MOD - 2, MOD) for i in range(m)]\n\n    # ----- 3. values that will be accumulated in the O(m) scan -----\n    # B_i = v_i * (2^{c_i}-1) * inv_prefix[i]\n    B = [0] * m\n    for i in range(m):\n        v = vals[i] % MOD\n        B[i] = v * nonempty[i] % MOD\n        B[i] = B[i] * inv_prefix[i] % MOD\n\n    # ----- 4. main O(m) contribution for pairs (p < q) -----\n    ans = 0\n    cum_B = 0                     # Σ_{p < current} B_p\n    for i in range(m):\n        v = vals[i] % MOD\n        v_sq = v * v % MOD\n        pref = prefix[i - 1] if i > 0 else 1          # Π_{k=0..i-1} 2^{c_k}\n        # A_i = v_i^2 * (2^{c_i}-1) * Π_{k=0..i-1} 2^{c_k}\n        A = v_sq * nonempty[i] % MOD\n        A = A * pref % MOD\n\n        ans = (ans + A * cum_B) % MOD                 # all pairs (p < i)\n        cum_B = (cum_B + B[i]) % MOD                  # add current B for later i\n\n    # ----- 5. add single‑value subsets (min = max) -----\n    for i in range(m):\n        v = vals[i] % MOD\n        v_cub = v * v % MOD * v % MOD\n        ans = (ans + v_cub * nonempty[i]) % MOD\n\n    return ans\n```\n\nThe function follows an O(N log N) approach (sorting + linear scan) and works for the maximal constraints (`len(nums) ≤ 10^5`). It returns the required sum modulo `10^9 + 7`.",
