      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minCoins(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    # 1‑indexed for convenience; prices[0] is dummy\n    p = [0] + prices\n    INF = 10**18\n    dp = [INF] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0                     # no fruits, no cost\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for k in range(1, i + 1):\n            if i <= k + k:          # buying fruit k covers up to k + k\n                prev = max(0, i - k)\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[prev] + p[k])\n\n    return dp[n]\n```\nThis function computes the minimal number of coins needed to acquire all fruits under the described offer.",
