      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    events = []\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(N):\n        t = int(input_data[idx])\n        x = int(input_data[idx+1])\n        events.append((t, x))\n        idx += 2\n\n    # Determine required potions: Find last occurrence of every type for each monster encounter\n    # Map each monster encounter to the latest possible potion occurrence\n    monster_indices = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for i in range(N - 1, -1, -1):\n        if events[i][0] == 2:\n            monster_indices[events[i][1]].append(i)\n    \n    # Store indices of type-1 events for each type\n    potion_indices = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for i in range(N):\n        if events[i][0] == 1:\n            potion_indices[events[i][1]].append(i)\n            \n    # Map each monster encounter to the index of the potion to be used\n    must_pick = [False] * N\n    for x in range(1, N + 1):\n        for m_idx in monster_indices[x]:\n            if not potion_indices[x] or potion_indices[x][-1] > m_idx:\n                print(\"-1\")\n                return\n            must_pick[potion_indices[x].pop()] = True\n\n    # Simulation to find K_min\n    # Use binary search on the number of potions allowed or simply simulate with a priority queue\n    # Actually, we need to pick only what's required and extra at each step if room allows? \n    # No, we must pick 'must_pick' potions. If we have room, we can pick others to help? \n    # Actually, the problem is to minimize the peak occupancy. \n    # We always pick 'must_pick'. To minimize peak, we should delay picking as much as possible, \n    # or just realize that picking any non-required potion only increases peak. \n    # So we only pick what is necessary.\n    \n    K = 0\n    curr = 0\n    events_with_must_pick = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        if events[i][0] == 1:\n            if must_pick[i]:\n                curr += 1\n                K = max(K, curr)\n        else:\n            curr -= 1\n            if curr < 0:\n                print(\"-1\")\n                return\n    \n    print(K)\n    print(*(1 if must_pick[i] else 0 for i in range(N) if events[i][0] == 1))\n\nsolve()\n```",
