      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef largest_polygon_perimeter(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the largest possible perimeter of a polygon that can be formed\n    from the elements of `nums`. If no polygon can be formed, return -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    nums.sort()                     # ascending order\n    prefix = 0                      # cumulative sum of processed elements\n    best = -1\n\n    # iterate from largest element downwards\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 1, 1, -1):\n        # prefix holds sum of nums[0..i-1]\n        if prefix > nums[i]:       # condition: sum of other sides > longest side\n            best = prefix + nums[i]\n            break                  # largest perimeter found\n        prefix += nums[i]          # add current element to prefix for next iteration\n\n    return best\n```\n\nThis function sorts the array, then scans from the largest side downward. The prefix sum keeps the total of the smaller sides. Whenever the prefix exceeds the current side, the polygon inequality holds, yielding the maximal perimeter. If the scan finishes without meeting the condition, `-1` is returned.",
