    "prediction": "gpt-oss-20b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef median_of_uniqueness(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the median of the uniqueness array of the given integer array `nums`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    n = len(nums)\n\n    # total number of subarrays\n    total_subarrays = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    # index of the required median (1‑based)\n    k = (total_subarrays + 1) // 2\n\n    def count_leq(limit: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Counts subarrays whose number of distinct elements is <= limit.\n        Uses a sliding window with a frequency dictionary.\n        \"\"\"\n        freq = {}\n        distinct = 0\n        left = 0\n        cnt = 0\n        for right, val in enumerate(nums):\n            freq[val] = freq.get(val, 0) + 1\n            if freq[val] == 1:\n                distinct += 1\n            # shrink window until distinct <= limit\n            while distinct > limit:\n                left_val = nums[left]\n                freq[left_val] -= 1\n                if freq[left_val] == 0:\n                    distinct -= 1\n                left += 1\n            # all subarrays ending at `right` and starting in [left, right]\n            cnt += right - left + 1\n        return cnt\n\n    # binary search for the smallest x such that count_leq(x) >= k\n    lo, hi = 1, n\n    ans = n\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if count_leq(mid) >= k:\n            ans = mid\n            hi = mid - 1\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n\n    return ans\n```\nThis function runs in `O(n log n)` time and `O(n)` auxiliary space, satisfying the constraints.",
