      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef leftoverAfterBuying(prices, money):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the amount of money left after buying exactly two chocolates\n    whose total price is as large as possible but does not exceed `money`.\n    If no such pair exists, returns `money`.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    prices : List[int]\n        List of chocolate prices.\n    money : int\n        Initial amount of money.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Remaining money after the purchase (or the original money if purchase is impossible).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(prices)\n    best_sum = -1  # best total price that fits within money\n\n    # Check all unordered pairs (i, j) with i < j\n    for i in range(n):\n        pi = prices[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            total = pi + prices[j]\n            if total <= money and total > best_sum:\n                best_sum = total\n\n    # If no suitable pair was found, return the original amount of money\n    if best_sum == -1:\n        return money\n    # Otherwise, return the leftover after spending the best possible sum\n    return money - best_sum\n```",
