      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n\n    # build children list (1-indexed)\n    children = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        p = int(next(it))\n        children[p].append(i)\n\n    # best coverage depth for each node (only policies with y>0 matter)\n    max_y = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(next(it))\n        y = int(next(it))\n        if y > max_y[x]:\n            max_y[x] = y\n\n    INF_NEG = -10**9\n    count = 0\n    stack = [(1, 0, INF_NEG)]          # (node, depth, max_up_ancestor)\n\n    while stack:\n        node, depth, max_up = stack.pop()\n        # value contributed by this node (if it has any policy)\n        up = depth + max_y[node] if max_y[node] > 0 else INF_NEG\n        cur_max = max(max_up, up)\n        if cur_max >= depth:\n            count += 1\n        for child in children[node]:\n            stack.append((child, depth + 1, cur_max))\n\n    print(count)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
