    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we can treat the indices as nodes in a graph. An edge exists between index `i` and `j` if `gcd(nums[i], nums[j]) > 1`. We need to check if the graph is connected. Since constructing the graph directly ($O(N^2)$) is too slow for $N=10^5$, we use a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) approach by associating numbers with their prime factors.\n\nEvery number `nums[i]` connects all its prime factors. If two numbers share a prime factor, they are in the same connected component. We iterate through each number, find its prime factors, and union the index `i` with the index of the prime factor in our DSU structure. Finally, we verify if all indices `i` where `nums[i] > 1` belong to the same component. (Indices where `nums[i] == 1` are isolated and must not exist if $N > 1$, or they are the only node if $N=1$).\n\n```python\ndef canTraverseAllPairs(nums: list[int]) -> bool:\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    if 1 in nums:\n        return False\n        \n    max_num = max(nums)\n    parent = list(range(n + max_num + 1))\n    \n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i:\n            return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n    \n    def union(i, j):\n        root_i = find(i)\n        root_j = find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j:\n            parent[root_i] = root_j\n            \n    # Precompute smallest prime factor (SPF) for fast factorization\n    spf = list(range(max_num + 1))\n    for i in range(2, int(max_num**0.5) + 1):\n        if spf[i] == i:\n            for j in range(i*i, max_num + 1, i):\n                if spf[j] == j:\n                    spf[j] = i\n                    \n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        temp = num\n        while temp > 1:\n            prime = spf[temp]\n            # Connect the index 'i' to the prime factor node\n            union(i, n + prime)\n            while temp % prime == 0:\n                temp //= prime\n                \n    # Check if all indices [0...n-1] share the same root\n    root = find(0)\n    return all(find(i) == root for i in range(1, n))\n```",
