      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom math import gcd\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef canTraverseAllPairs(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    \n    # Build graph using prime factorization\n    # Each number connects to its prime factors\n    # Numbers share an edge if they share a prime factor\n    \n    # Map prime -> list of indices that have this prime\n    prime_to_indices = defaultdict(list)\n    \n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        # Get prime factors of num\n        temp = num\n        d = 2\n        while d * d <= temp:\n            if temp % d == 0:\n                prime_to_indices[d].append(i)\n                while temp % d == 0:\n                    temp //= d\n            d += 1\n        if temp > 1:\n            prime_to_indices[temp].append(i)\n    \n    # Union-Find to group indices connected by common primes\n    parent = list(range(n))\n    rank = [0] * n\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n    \n    # Connect all indices that share a prime factor\n    for prime, indices in prime_to_indices.items():\n        for i in range(1, len(indices)):\n            union(indices[0], indices[i])\n    \n    # Check if all indices belong to the same component\n    root = find(0)\n    return all(find(i) == root for i in range(1, n))\n```",
