    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W, N = map(int, data[0].split())\n    T = data[1].strip()\n    grid = [line.strip() for line in data[2:2+H]]\n    \n    # Find all possible starting positions (land cells not on perimeter)\n    possible_starts = []\n    for i in range(1, H-1):\n        for j in range(1, W-1):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                possible_starts.append((i, j))\n    \n    # For each possible start, simulate the path and check if all steps are on land\n    possible_ends = set()\n    \n    for start_i, start_j in possible_starts:\n        i, j = start_i, start_j\n        valid = True\n        # Simulate the entire path\n        for move in T:\n            if move == 'L':\n                j -= 1\n            elif move == 'R':\n                j += 1\n            elif move == 'U':\n                i -= 1\n            elif move == 'D':\n                i += 1\n            # Check if the new position is land and not sea\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                valid = False\n                break\n        if valid:\n            possible_ends.add((i, j))\n    \n    print(len(possible_ends))\n\nsolve()\n```",
