      "generated_answer": "We are given:\n\n- P(D) = 0.05 (incidence of disease)\n- P(TP | D) = 0.99 (probability of testing positive given disease)\n- P(TN | ¬D) = 0.97 → P(TP | ¬D) = 1 - 0.97 = 0.03 (false positive rate)\n\nWe want P(D | TP), which by Bayes' theorem is:\n\nP(D | TP) = [P(TP | D) * P(D)] / [P(TP | D) * P(D) + P(TP | ¬D) * P(¬D)]  \n= (0.99 * 0.05) / (0.99 * 0.05 + 0.03 * 0.95)  \n= 0.0495 / (0.0495 + 0.0285) = 0.0495 / 0.078 ≈ 0.6346\n\nSo, P(D | TP) ≈ 0.635\n\n\\boxed{F}",
