    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given a Bayesian network with the structure: H → U ← P ← W. This means:\n\n- H influences U,\n- P influences U,\n- W influences P.\n\nSo the dependencies are:\n- P depends on W,\n- U depends on both H and P,\n- H and W are root nodes (no parents).\n\nAssume all variables are binary (common assumption unless specified otherwise).\n\nNow, count the independent parameters:\n\n1. H: as a root node with no parents, needs 1 parameter (P(H)).\n2. W: also a root node, needs 1 parameter (P(W)).\n3. P: depends on W. Since W is binary, P has two cases: P(P|W=0) and P(P|W=1), each needing 1 parameter → 2 parameters.\n4. U: depends on H and P. Both H and P are binary, so U has 2×2 = 4 combinations of parents. For each, we need one parameter (e.g., P(U=1|H,P)) → 4 parameters.\n\nTotal independent parameters: 1 (H) + 1 (W) + 2 (P|W) + 4 (U|H,P) = 8.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 163,
        "output_tokens": 264,
        "total_tokens": 427
