      "generated_answer": "Statement 1: The set of all rectangles (including non-axis-aligned) in the 2D plane cannot shatter 5 points. The VC-dimension of rectangles in the plane is 5, meaning they can shatter some sets of 5 points, but not any arbitrary set — however, typically the VC-dimension is considered as the maximum number for which there exists at least one set of that size that can be shattered. But for arbitrary rectangles (rotated allowed), the VC-dimension is actually 5, so they *can* shatter some set of 5 points. Thus, the statement is **True** in the sense that there exists a set of 5 points that can be shattered.\n\nStatement 2: The 1-Nearest Neighbor (1-NN) classifier can perfectly fit any labeling of a finite dataset (as it memorizes the training data), meaning it can shatter datasets of arbitrary size in theory. Hence, its VC-dimension is infinite. This makes the second statement **True**.\n\nTherefore, both statements are True.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
