    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "A standard roulette wheel has numbers from 1 to 36. The sum of these numbers can be calculated using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series: $ S = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l) $, where $ n = 36 $, $ a = 1 $, and $ l = 36 $. This gives $ S = \\frac{36}{2}(1 + 36) = 18 \\times 37 = 666 $. Therefore, the sum of all the numbers on a roulette wheel is indeed 666.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
