    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The forced-choice method requires raters to select from pairs of statements (e.g., \"works hard\" vs. \"is friendly\") where one is organizationally desirable and the other is not. This structure forces the rater to choose based on predefined criteria rather than personal impressions, which significantly reduces halo effect and leniency/severity bias. Therefore, the primary advantage is its ability to produce more objective and reliable ratings.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
