      "generated_answer": "Carl Rogers' theory emphasizes the concept of self-structure and the importance of congruence between one's experiences and self-concept. When an individual's actions contradict deeply held beliefs about themselves or their family, it creates incongruence, leading to psychological distress. In this case, Peter's parents have a self-structure tied to the belief that male family members must be doctors to have value, and Peter's choice as an artist challenges this, creating internal conflict despite their love for him.\n\nThus, the best explanation according to Rogers is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
