    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Explicit collusion refers to firms openly and directly agreeing to cooperate, such as setting prices or output levels, often through direct communication. Tacit collusion, on the other hand, occurs when firms coordinate their behavior—like maintaining high prices—without any formal agreement, often by observing and mimicking each other’s actions in an oligopolistic market. The key distinction is that explicit collusion involves direct communication or agreements, while tacit collusion does not, making option A the most accurate description.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
