    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The federal budget deficit refers to the amount by which government spending exceeds revenue in a single fiscal year, while the federal debt is the total accumulation of all past deficits (and any surpluses). Therefore, the debt grows when there is a deficit and shrinks when there is a surplus (a negative deficit). This means that when the deficit is negative (a surplus), the debt decreases.\n\nThe only option that correctly reflects this relationship is C: \"When the deficit is negative the debt decreases.\"\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
