      "generated_answer": "For a Durbin-Watson test with $n=50$ and $k'=2$ (two explanatory variables excluding the constant), the critical values at a 5% significance level are approximately $d_L = 1.46$ and $d_U = 1.63$. Since the calculated statistic of 1.53 falls between $d_L$ and $d_U$, the test does not provide sufficient evidence to either reject or fail to reject the null hypothesis of no autocorrelation. Therefore, the result is inconclusive.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
