      "generated_answer": "The candidate has raised a federal constitutional claim against state election officials, which falls within the jurisdiction of the federal court under 28 U.S.C. § 1331. However, when a federal court is asked to rule on a federal constitutional challenge to a state statute that is currently being interpreted by a state court in ongoing proceedings, the abstention doctrine—specifically Burford or Younger abstention—may apply to avoid unnecessary friction between state and federal courts. Given that the state court has already scheduled a prompt hearing and intends to rule quickly on the interpretation of its own statute, the federal court should abstain from intervening until the state court has had the opportunity to clarify the statutory issue.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
