      "generated_answer": "The \"boomerang effect\" occurs when a persuasive message backfires, causing people to adopt an attitude or behavior opposite to what was intended. Injunctive messages, which communicate societal norms about what behaviors are approved or disapproved, can sometimes trigger psychological reactance, leading individuals to resist the message and engage in the discouraged behavior more strongly. Thus, an injunctive message might unintentionally amplify the negative outcome it seeks to prevent due to this boomerang effect.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{boomerang effect}}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 98,
        "output_tokens": 107,
        "total_tokens": 205
      },
