      "generated_answer": "The seven roots of unity are \\(x_k=\\omega^{k}\\) \\((k=0,\\dots ,6)\\).  \nWe need \\(\\displaystyle P=\\prod_{k=0}^{6}\\bigl(x_k^{3}+x_k+1\\bigr)\n=\\operatorname{Res}(x^{7}-1,\\;x^{3}+x+1)\\).\n\nLet \\(r_1,r_2,r_3\\) be the roots of \\(x^{3}+x+1=0\\).  \nFor such a root \\(r\\), \\(r^{3}=-r-1\\).  Using this repeatedly:\n\n\\[\nr^{7}=r^{6}r=(r^{3})^{2}r=(-r-1)^{2}r=r^{3}+2r^{2}+r\n=(-r-1)+2r^{2}+r=2r^{2}-1,\n\\]\nhence \\(r^{7}-1=2r^{2}-2=2(r^{2}-1)\\).\n\nThus\n\n\\[\nP=\\prod_{i=1}^{3}\\!\\bigl(r_i^{7}-1\\bigr)=2^{3}\\prod_{i=1}^{3}(r_i^{2}-1)\n=8\\,\\Bigl(\\prod_{i}(r_i-1)\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\prod_{i}(r_i+1)\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(f(x)=x^{3}+x+1\\),\n\n\\[\n\\prod_{i}(r_i-1)=(-1)^{3}f(1)=-3,\\qquad\n\\prod_{i}(r_i+1)=(-1)^{3}f(-1)=1.\n\\]\n\nTherefore  \n\\[\nP=8\\cdot(-3)\\cdot1=-24.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-24}\n\\]",
