      "generated_answer": "We compute the function values for small indices to find a pattern.  \nFor \\(i = 0\\), \\(f(0, j) \\equiv j+1 \\pmod{5}\\), giving the cycle \\(1,2,3,4,0\\).  \nFor \\(i \\ge 1\\), we find that \\(f(i, j) = (j+1)^{2^i} \\bmod 5\\) for \\(j=1,2,3,4\\), and using Fermat's little theorem \\((j+1)^4 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\\) when \\(j+1 \\not\\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}\\), we determine \\(2^{2015} \\bmod 4 = 0\\), so \\(f(2015,2) \\equiv 3^{2^{2015}} \\equiv 3^4 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5}\\).\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
