    "global index": "MathQA_782",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: each of 3 investments has a 20 % of becoming worthless within a year of purchase , independently of what happens to the other two investments . if simone invests an equal sum k in each of these 3 investments on january 1 , the approximate chance that by the end of the year , she loses no more than 1 / 3 of her original investment is\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 %\nB. 80 %\nC. 70 %\nD. 60 %\nE. 40 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are told that each investment has a 20% (0.2) chance of becoming worthless independently, so the probability that an investment *does not* become worthless is 80% (0.8). Simone invests equal amounts in 3 investments, so her total investment is $3k$. Losing no more than $1/3$ of her original investment means she loses at most $k$, which happens if at most one investment fails (since each is worth $k$).\n\nWe compute the probability that 0 or 1 of the 3 investments become worthless:\n- P(0 fail) = $ (0.8)^3 = 0.512 $\n- P(1 fails) = $ \\binom{3}{1} (0.2)(0.8)^2 = 3 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.64 = 0.384 $\n- Total ≈ $ 0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896 $, or about 90%.\n\nThus, the approximate chance is 90%.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 194,
        "output_tokens": 241,
        "total_tokens": 435
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
