    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: each of 3 investments has a 20 % of becoming worthless within a year of purchase , independently of what happens to the other two investments . if simone invests an equal sum k in each of these 3 investments on january 1 , the approximate chance that by the end of the year , she loses no more than 1 / 3 of her original investment is\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 %\nB. 80 %\nC. 70 %\nD. 60 %\nE. 40 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "xiaomi/mimo-v2.5",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Simone invests $k$ in each of 3 investments, so the total original investment is $3k$. Losing no more than $1/3$ of the original investment means the total loss must be at most $k$. Since each investment either becomes worthless (loss of $k$) or not (loss of $0$), the total loss can be $0$, $k$, $2k$, or $3k$. The condition is satisfied only if the total loss is $0$ or $k$, which corresponds to at most one investment becoming worthless. The probability that none become worthless is $(0.8)^3 = 0.512$, and the probability that exactly one becomes worthless is $\\binom{3}{1}(0.2)(0.8)^2 = 0.384$. Adding these gives $0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896$, which is approximately $90\\%$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
