      "generated_answer": "Let $x$ be the length of one piece of the wire, meaning the other piece has length $12-x$. The length of the longer piece is $L = \\max(x, 12-x)$, and the resulting square has side length $L/4$, so the area is $(L/4)^2 = L^2/16$. We require $L^2/16 > 4$, which simplifies to $L^2 > 64$, or $L > 8$. Solving for $x$, we find the condition is satisfied if $x > 8$ (when $x$ is the longer piece) or $12-x > 8$ (when $12-x$ is the longer piece), which gives $x \\in [0, 4) \\cup (8, 12]$. Since the total length of the wire is 12, the probability is $(4 + 4) / 12 = 8 / 12 = 2 / 3$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
