      "generated_answer": "Martingales are stochastic processes where the conditional expectation of the next value, given the present, equals the current value, making the Azéma supermartingale a key example subject to Kurtz's theorem. The theorem links convergence to the self-adjointness of the generator, often denoted as the \"Z-hat t\" operator in this context. This framework is fundamental in probability theory for analyzing limit behaviors.\n\n\\boxed{Martingales}",
