    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We start with the Laplace transform of $ f(t) = e^{kt} $, which is $ \\mathcal{L}\\{e^{kt}\\} = \\frac{1}{s - k} $ for $ \\text{Re}(s) > \\text{Re}(k) $. Using the identities:\n\n- $ \\cosh(kt) = \\frac{e^{kt} + e^{-kt}}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathcal{L}\\{\\cosh(kt)\\} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{s - k} + \\frac{1}{s + k} \\right) = \\frac{s}{s^2 - k^2} $\n- $ \\sinh(kt) = \\frac{e^{kt} - e^{-kt}}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathcal{L}\\{\\sinh(kt)\\} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{1}{s - k} - \\frac{1}{s + k} \\right) = \\frac{k}{s^2 - k^2} $\n- $ \\cos(kt) = \\frac{e^{ikt} + e^{-ikt}}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathcal{L}\\{\\cos(kt)\\} = \\frac{s}{s^2 + k^2} $\n- $ \\sin(kt) = \\frac{e^{ikt} - e^{-ikt}}{2} \\Rightarrow \\mathcal{L}\\{\\sin(kt)\\} = \\frac{k}{s^2 + k^2} $\n\nComparing these results with the options, only option **J** matches all four transforms exactly.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
