    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the energy stored in an inductor from t = 0 to t = 1 whose \\textphi -icharacteristic is given by \\textphi (t) = 1/3i^3 (t) and the current through it is given by i (t) = 2 sin t.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.00 J\nB. 0.75 J\nC. 1.50 J\nD. 4.00 J\nE. 2.50 J\nF. 3.00 J\nG. 1.25 J\nH. 2.75 J\nI. 2.00 J\nJ. 3.50 J\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The energy stored in an inductor is given by $ W = \\int_0^t v(t) i(t) \\, dt $. The voltage across the inductor is $ v(t) = \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} $, and since $ \\phi(t) = \\frac{1}{3} i^3(t) $, we compute $ v(t) = \\frac{d}{dt} \\left( \\frac{1}{3} i^3(t) \\right) = i^2(t) \\cdot \\frac{di}{dt} $. Given $ i(t) = 2\\sin t $, then $ i^2(t) = 4\\sin^2 t $, and $ \\frac{di}{dt} = 2\\cos t $, so $ v(t) = 4\\sin^2 t \\cdot 2\\cos t = 8\\sin^2 t \\cos t $. Then $ v(t)i(t) = 8\\sin^2 t \\cos t \\cdot 2\\sin t = 16\\sin^3 t \\cos t $. Now integrate from 0 to 1:  \n$$\nW = \\int_0^1 16\\sin^3 t \\cos t \\, dt\n$$\nLet $ u = \\sin t $, $ du = \\cos t\\, dt $, so when $ t = 0 $, $ u = 0 $; $ t = 1 $, $ u = \\sin 1 $. Then:\n$$\nW = 16 \\int_0^{\\sin 1} u^3 \\, du = 16 \\cdot \\left[ \\frac{u^4}{4} \\right]_0^{\\sin 1} = 4 \\sin^4(1)\n$$\nNow $ \\sin(1) \\approx \\sin(57.3^\\circ) \\approx 0.8415 $, so $ \\sin^4(1) \\approx (0.8415)^4 \\approx 0.500 $, then $ W \\approx 4 \\cdot 0.5 = 2.00 \\, \\text{J} $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
