    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10076",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Five resistances of 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 ohms are connected in parallel. Calculate the joint resistance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.46 ohms\nB. 4.56 ohms\nC. 8.23 ohms\nD. 4.12 ohms\nE. 6.78 ohms\nF. 7.89 ohms\nG. 1.92 ohms\nH. 2.34 ohms\nI. 2.21 ohms\nJ. 5.67 ohms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the joint resistance (equivalent resistance) of resistors in parallel, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3} + \\frac{1}{R_4} + \\frac{1}{R_5}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30}\n$$\n\nFinding a common denominator (LCM of 10, 15, 20, 25, 30 is 300):\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{30}{300} + \\frac{20}{300} + \\frac{15}{300} + \\frac{12}{300} + \\frac{10}{300} = \\frac{87}{300}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\nR_{eq} = \\frac{300}{87} \\approx 3.448\\ \\text{ohms} \\approx 3.46\\ \\text{ohms}\n$$\n\nThe closest option is **A. 3.46 ohms**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 220,
        "output_tokens": 333,
        "total_tokens": 553
      },
