      "generated_answer": "To find the equivalent resistance of resistors in parallel, we use the formula:  \n\\[\n\\frac{1}{R_{\\text{eq}}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3} + \\frac{1}{R_4} + \\frac{1}{R_5}.\n\\]  \nSubstituting the given values \\(10, 15, 20, 25, 30\\) ohms:  \n\\[\n\\frac{1}{R_{\\text{eq}}} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30} = 0.1 + 0.0667 + 0.05 + 0.04 + 0.0333 = 0.29.\n\\]  \nThus, \\(R_{\\text{eq}} = \\frac{1}{0.29} \\approx 3.448\\) ohms, which matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
