    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To represent 110 distinct codewords, we need $n$ bits such that $2^n \\ge 110$, which results in $n=7$ bits because $2^6 = 64$ and $2^7 = 128$. The efficiency is calculated as the ratio of the information content required ($\\log_2 110 \\approx 6.78$) to the total capacity provided by the bits used ($\\log_2 128 = 7$), resulting in approximately $6.78/7 \\approx 96.8\\%$, which rounds to 97 percent. Thus, 7 bits are required with an efficiency of 97 percent.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
