    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_5473",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The pancreas secretes a large amount of digestive enzymes after a meal. Which statement about this process is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Bile is needed to activate all pancreatic enzymes\nB. All pancreatic enzymes are produced in an active form and can start digestion immediately\nC. Enzymes are produced in the pancreas but released in the stomach for digestion\nD. Pepsinogen is the chief enzyme which digests protein and requires removal of a peptide sequence from the active cleft before it can work\nE. Pancreatic secretion of hydrochloric acid is required to provide the correct pH for maximal pancreatic enzyme in the duodenum\nF. Enteropeptidase converts trypsinogen to trypsin by cleavage of a peptide sequence that blocks the active site of trypsin.\nG. Pancreatic enzymes are needed to break down carbohydrates only.\nH. Pancreatic á-amylase will hydrolyse starch to free glucose\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The pancreas secretes digestive enzymes in inactive forms (zymogens) to prevent autodigestion, and these are activated in the duodenum. The key activation event is the conversion of trypsinogen to trypsin by enteropeptidase, an enzyme in the duodenal mucosa, which cleaves a peptide sequence blocking the active site. Trypsin then activates other pancreatic enzymes, making option F correct.\n\nOther options are incorrect: bile does not activate all enzymes (A), pancreatic enzymes are not secreted in active form (B), they are not released in the stomach (C), pepsinogen is gastric, not pancreatic (D), the pancreas does not secrete HCl (E), pancreatic enzymes digest more than just carbohydrates (G), and pancreatic amylase produces maltose and oligosaccharides, not free glucose (H).\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
