      "generated_answer": "A grid in radiography is used to reduce scattered (secondary) radiation, improving image contrast by absorbing this scatter before it reaches the film. However, because the grid also absorbs some primary radiation, a higher exposure (mAs) is typically required to compensate, which increases patient dose. Therefore, the main disadvantage is increased patient exposure due to the need for more exposure time or higher technique.\n\nThe correct answer is:  \n\\boxed{A}",
