    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Thiopental is a barbiturate with a very short duration of action after a single dose, primarily due to its rapid redistribution from the brain to other tissues, especially adipose tissue. While high lipid solubility (C) allows it to cross the blood-brain barrier quickly, the key reason for the short duration is the rapid movement out of the brain and into fat stores, which reduces brain concentrations swiftly. This redistribution, not metabolism, is the main factor, making rapid accumulation in body fat the best answer.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
