  {
    "global index": "MedMCQA_511",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A lateral sliding flap done on a tooth with roots denuded for 6 years will show\n\nOptions: \nA. PDL fibres attached to cementum\nB. PDL fibres attached to dentin\nC. Epithelium adjacent to previously denuded root surface\nD. Co adaptation to the remaining fibres\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When a root surface has been denuded for a long period (like 6 years), the cementum is altered, often contaminated, and unsuitable for new connective tissue attachment. Consequently, the healing process results in a long junctional epithelium forming between the flap and the root surface rather than new periodontal ligament fibers. Therefore, the histological finding will be epithelium.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 136,
        "output_tokens": 205,
