    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, insulin deficiency leads to decreased activity of lipoprotein lipase (which requires insulin for full activity) and increased activity of hormone-sensitive lipase in adipose tissue due to unopposed action of counter-regulatory hormones. This results in increased free fatty acid flux to the liver, which promotes hepatic synthesis and secretion of VLDL, thereby elevating triglyceride and VLDL levels. Therefore, the correct answer is increased hormone-sensitive lipase activity and decreased lipoprotein lipase activity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
