    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When both parts of a musical phrase are developed from the same motif, this typically indicates that the second part is a variation or sequential transformation of the first, which is characteristic of parallel phrasing. Parallel phrasing involves using similar melodic material in both segments of the phrase, often with the same rhythmic and contour structure but possibly transposed or altered slightly. This is distinct from balanced phrasing (which uses different but harmonically or structurally complementary ideas) or mere labeling as a+b (which denotes contrasting ideas).\n\nThus, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
